<title>USA: Lehman reprices 2001 maturity on D.C. $73 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Lehman reprices 2001 maturity on D.C. $73 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Tuesday it repriced District of Columbia's $72.7 million Georgetown University bonds, adjusting yields in several maturities and leaving the top yield in 2018 unchanged at 6.07 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>District of Columbia</p>
<p>RE: $72,650,000*</p>
<p>University Revenue Refunding Bonds</p>
<p>(Georgetown University Issue)</p>
<p>Series 1998 A</p>
<p>Verbal award.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA	MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 01/06/1998	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 04/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>04/01/1999		  705M    4.65  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2000		1,780M    5.50  %	  4.85</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 101.353)</p>
<p>04/01/2001		1,905M    5.50  %	  5.00</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 101.468)</p>
<p>04/01/2002		2,035M    6.00  %	  5.10</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 103.38 )</p>
<p>04/01/2003		2,180M    6.00  %	  5.15</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 103.848)</p>
